WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.645
Cognitive Load Theory helps designers build learning experiences that respect working

00:00:04.645 --> 00:00:05.480
memory limits.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.070
Learners can only process so much new information at once,

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.355
especially when they lack schemas for the domain.

00:00:10.355 --> 00:00:14.296
Strong design supports the movement from limited working memory activity to organized

00:00:14.296 --> 00:00:16.835
long-term knowledge that learners can retrieve and use.

00:00:16.835 --> 00:00:21.715
A major takeaway is to distinguish necessary difficulty from unnecessary difficulty.

00:00:21.715 --> 00:00:25.040
Intrinsic load comes from the task itself and must be managed through sequencing,

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.844
chunking, scaffolding, and progressive complexity.

00:00:27.844 --> 00:00:31.300
Extraneous load comes from confusing or inefficient instruction and should be reduced

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.715
wherever possible.

00:00:32.715 --> 00:00:35.445
Productive mental effort should go toward understanding, schema building,

00:00:35.445 --> 00:00:36.505
and skill development.

00:00:36.505 --> 00:00:40.445
Worked examples, guided practice, feedback, signaling, purposeful multimedia,

00:00:40.445 --> 00:00:43.200
and adaptive support all help manage load.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.735
Beginners often need more structure.

00:00:44.735 --> 00:00:45.995
As learners gain expertise,

00:00:45.995 --> 00:00:49.435
guidance should fade and practice should become more varied and realistic.

00:00:49.435 --> 00:00:51.880
The design should evolve as the learner's knowledge changes.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.060
The goal is not to make learning effortless.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.055
Effort is part of learning.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.170
The goal is to make effort focused, productive,

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:59.680
and connected to real understanding and performance.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.505
When instruction respects cognitive load,

00:01:01.505 --> 00:01:05.115
learners are more likely to see the important relationships, build usable schemas,

00:01:05.115 --> 00:01:06.880
and carry the skill back into real work.
